@* Vertical is CSS: writing-mode on the input, and the browser turns its own track and thumb with
   it. The keys follow — Up increases — with nothing bound.

   Two of them at h-40, as upstream shows it: one slider on its own reads as a scrollbar, and it
   takes a second one beside it to read as a pair of controls. *@
<div class="mx-auto flex h-40 w-full max-w-xs items-center justify-center gap-6">
    <Slider name="left" Orientation="vertical" Value="50" Class="h-full" aria-label="Left" />
    <Slider name="right" Orientation="vertical" Value="25" Class="h-full" aria-label="Right" />
</div>
